From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:16:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: multisampled texel fetches, varyings after the
 depth test, a native code self-test

Texel fetches from a multisampled texture read the sample's place in the pixel's grid (its
texels decoded as multisampled render targets are drawn: a grid of samples a pixel).

Varyings are interpolated after the early depth test, not for blocks it rejects.

EDEN_SW_JIT_TEST=1 runs each instruction native code does on awkward values (NaNs, infinities,
zeros of both signs, denormals, edge integers) against the interpreter, and logs how many
differ. It found the logical instructions assuming their operands were 0 or 1; they now treat
any value but 0 as true, as the interpreter does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7DVAudgDzMpBqJZHAz
---
